{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Therefore.</b> <b>Its throat.</b> It is the spirit that goes out of the mouth, and like it: נפשו גחלים תלהט (Job 41:14)." "<b>And it opens wide.</b> Like פתחה (opened), and like it: ופיהם פערו למלקוש [Job 29:23]." "<b>Without restraint.</b> The opposite of custom." "<b>And revelry.</b> And all revelry that is in it. Or it may be that others will revel at its downfall. And Rabbi Jonah, of blessed memory, says that it is like the laughter that happens to some of the dying at the time of death."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:55.883238096Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}